From: andrewheathcote <ajheathcote@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:51:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] dev-nle M0: flow_scaled cards register in R, card format
 v1, golden checks, verify script

- register_nn_model() reads the scaled DDM card (DDMnle) as kind
  "flow_scaled": DDM's parameterisation, bounds, zero exceptions and
  simulator; R path nn_eval_scaled() (the NLE reference ddm_sc_density
  with SZ as the proportion); the compiled path is the patched evaluator
  (nn_native_spec passes scaled = TRUE and sc_pars). No scaffold card.
  Compiled vs R path <= 2.3e-12 over 200 prior draws in each of the six
  regimes; oracle (network replaced by the analytic unit-scale DDM) 8e-14
  at st0 = 0.
- Card versions: card_version (absent = 0), versions 0 and 1 read, any
  other refused by name; structured `scaling`; `support`, `mass_tolerance`,
  `beyond_support` read by nn_total_mass(); `control_limits` for race cards
  (warned about by nn_cell / nn_in_box); a v1 card without `validation`
  registers with a message. vignette("neural-likelihood-cards") is the spec.
- nn_golden_check(): a card against its golden vectors, one PASS/FAIL line;
  the shipped artefacts' golden files are installed with them.
  inst/scripts/nle_verify.R runs every check and exits non-zero on a FAIL.
- nn_sz_convert(): the SZ conventions (proportion / width) as a contract,
  with a golden row at each boundary in the tests.
- The training-region rule warns and never enforces (nn_in_box(error =
  TRUE) for the old behaviour); make_emc() warns when t0 is sampled and
  rt_resolution is coarser than 1 ms (the flooring applies with
  compress = FALSE too).
- R < 4.5: MANIFEST carries md5 lines, so the shipped artefacts load where
  tools::sha256sum does not exist; a missing pin is refused by name.
- ?DDMnn: the cap256w_c4 t0 shift is recorded as unresolved, no correction
  applied; the scaled card replaces it for the variability models.
- tests: test-nn-scaled.R (random-weight fixture always; the real DDMnle
  card with EMC2_NLE_SCALED_CARD), test-nn-golden.R; the NLE reference
  ddm_scaled.R in tests/testthat/port. test-nn-*: 919 expectations, 0
  failures, on R 4.3.3.

