@@ -0,0 +1,69 @@
+% Generated by roxygen2: do not edit by hand
+% Please edit documentation in R/nn_golden.R
+\name{nn_golden_check}
+\alias{nn_golden_check}
+\title{Check a Neural Likelihood Against Its Golden Vectors}
+\usage{
+nn_golden_check(
+  x,
+  golden = NULL,
+  tol = 1e-09,
+  flow_only = FALSE,
+  error = TRUE,
+  twin = NULL,
+  ...
+)
+}
+\arguments{
+\item{x}{A model function from \code{\link[=register_nn_model]{register_nn_model()}}, its model list, a
+registration, a card path, or a shipped artefact's name.}
+
+\item{golden}{Path of the golden CSV. Default: the file beside the card,
+or the shipped one.}
+
+\item{tol}{The largest absolute difference accepted, per output
+(\code{log_pdf} and the CDF). The exporters' float64 port and EMC2 agree to
+about \code{1e-12}; \code{1e-9} leaves room for a different BLAS. A LAN converted
+from a float32 ONNX file needs about \code{1e-4}.}
+
+\item{flow_only}{For a joint flow: compare the flow's part only (the joint
+log density minus \code{log_p_R}, and the CDF divided by \code{P(R)}), for a golden
+file written with another classifier than the card's.}
+
+\item{error}{If \code{TRUE} (the default), a failed check is an error; otherwise
+the result is returned with \code{pass = FALSE}.}
+
+\item{twin, ...}{Passed to \code{\link[=register_nn_model]{register_nn_model()}} when \code{x} is a path or a name.}
+}
+\value{
+(Invisibly) an \code{nn_golden_check} object: \code{label}, \code{kind}, \code{n} rows,
+\code{max_abs} (the largest difference per output), \code{tol}, \code{pass}. Its print
+method is one line, \code{PASS} or \code{FAIL} with the largest difference.
+}
+\description{
+Evaluates the network of a registered neural likelihood (see
+\code{\link[=register_nn_model]{register_nn_model()}}) on the parameter vectors and times of its golden
+file and compares the outputs with the values recorded there. The golden
+file is written by the exporter from the trained weights (the NLE project's
+\code{export_flow*.py}, or \code{golden.py} from a card), so this is the test that
+the installed evaluator is the network the card describes: a wrong input
+order, transform, constant or spline setting fails it by a large margin.
+}
+\details{
+The golden file is a CSV with one row per (parameter set, time):
+for race flows the columns \code{param_id}, the inputs in \code{context_names} order
+on the network's scale, \code{rt}, \code{log_pdf}, \code{cdf}, \code{log_sf}; for joint flows
+(\code{flow_joint}, \code{flow_scaled}) the inputs on the exporter's storage scale
+(the sampled scale; for a \code{zerobox} input the log, or the probit for \code{SZ},
+of the natural value, \code{-Inf} at an exact zero), \code{R}, \code{rt}, \code{log_pdf_joint},
+\code{cdf_defective} and \code{log_p_R}; for a LAN (\code{mlp_joint}) the inputs on the
+natural scale, \code{rt}, \code{choice} or \code{R}, and the log density. For a
+\code{flow_scaled} card \code{rt} is the unit-scale time \code{u}.
+
+Shipped artefacts carry their golden files in
+\code{system.file("extdata", "flownn", "golden", package = "EMC2")}; a card
+\verb{<tag>_weights.json} is checked against \verb{<tag>_golden.csv} beside it.
+}
+\examples{
+nn_golden_check("rdm_small")
+}
