+% Generated by roxygen2: do not edit by hand
+% Please edit documentation in R/nn_register.R
+\name{nn_sz_convert}
+\alias{nn_sz_convert}
+\title{Convert Between the Start-Point Variability Conventions}
+\usage{
+nn_sz_convert(
+  x,
+  Z,
+  from = c("proportion", "width"),
+  to = c("width", "proportion")
+)
+}
+\arguments{
+\item{x}{Values in the \code{from} convention.}
+
+\item{Z}{The relative start point, natural scale in (0, 1), recycled.}
+
+\item{from, to}{The conventions.}
+}
+\value{
+\code{x} in the \code{to} convention.
+}
+\description{
+Three conventions for the DDM's start-point variability are in use, and
+every interface states which it takes:
+\itemize{
+\item \code{"proportion"}: EMC2's natural-scale \code{SZ}, a proportion in \verb{[0, 1)} of
+the width available at the start point \code{Z}; the value a model's
+\code{p_types}/\code{transform} produce from the sampled probit, what the
+simulator takes, and the input of the shipped DDM flows and the scaled
+DDM card (\code{scaling$sz = "proportion"}).
+\item \code{"width"}: the absolute relative width \code{sw = 2 * SZ * min(Z, 1 - Z)}
+that \code{\link[=DDM]{DDM()}}'s \code{Ttransform} passes to its likelihood (WienR's \code{sw}).
+}
+}
+\details{
+The two are exact inverses of each other at a given \code{Z}.
+}
+\examples{
+nn_sz_convert(0.2, Z = 0.3, from = "proportion", to = "width")   # 2 * 0.2 * 0.3
+nn_sz_convert(0.12, Z = 0.3, from = "width", to = "proportion")
+}
